  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm the r1 gate and 021, 022, 034; read SearchResultsWidget's props and map 022's structuredContent onto them (note gaps).</step>
    <step order="2">Write SearchResultsWidgetResource, register it, add the embed and CI steps, set resourceUri on 022's tools.</step>
    <step order="3">Scaffold spaarke-search-results; write App.test.tsx; build; run check-bundle-size.mjs.</step>
    <step order="4">Run the AI.Widgets tests, MCP suites, ArchTests and conformance; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="6">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the bundle exceeds 3 MB, STOP and escalate.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>SearchResultsWidget (Spaarke.AI.Widgets); r1/034 widget scaffold and resource pattern; notes/reuse-scan.md row "Search results component" (props only).</existing>
    <extension>The component is reused unchanged; a new resource and widget folder are required because each MCP App widget is a separate ui:// single-file resource (owner Q5).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Search results appear only as text in Copilot, and FR-16's search-results widget acceptance fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Search results widget in Copilot Chat and Cowork">
      <steps>
        <step>After deploy 039, ask "Find Spaarke documents about indemnification" with the Spaarke MCP source</step>
        <step>Verify the widget lists hits with names, matters and snippets; activate a hit with the keyboard and confirm the host opens the link</step>
        <step>Repeat in Cowork; check the widget console for errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Hits render and open; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the host to dark theme</step>
        <step>Verify the widget follows the host theme</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Fluent v9 semantic tokens only</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">build, jest and check-bundle-size in src/client/widgets/spaarke-search-results</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build; dotnet test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Search/SearchResultsWidgetResource.cs</output>
